Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.17,0:00:07.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}A puzzle. How many cars\Ncross this line each hour?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.55,0:00:12.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}No clock. Just one photo from above,\Nwhere every speedometer can be read.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.68,0:00:17.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Can one photo, with no time\Nin it, give you a rate?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.63,0:00:24.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}It can. Draw a thin strip around the line.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.18,0:00:30.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}A fast car spends little time inside,\Nso catching one there counts for more.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.14,0:00:35.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Add up the speeds of the cars inside,\Nand divide by the strip's width.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.00,0:00:39.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}On average, that is how\Nmany cars cross per hour.
